    "articles": [
      {
        "sequence_id": 1,
        "text": "B. Free Interchange of Past and Present Tense Subjunctive\n\nThe Past form is often used instead of the Present form and vice versa in both speaking and writing where it is felt that when subjunctive and indicative forms are identical the meaning might be obscured:\nEr sagte, alles, was er wisse, sei, dass er nichts wisse; viele wüssten aber auch dieses nicht.\nWüssten is used here because the Present form would be identical with the indicative wissen.\nNote that there is not a trace of past meaning to the past form.  It fits in quite naturally with the Present forms.\n"
      }
    ],
